# Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)

Every public component in all five runtimes must meet **WCAG 2.2 Level AA** before it is considered done. Parity includes accessibility — not just visual DOM.

## Baseline requirements (all components)

- **Keyboard operable** — all interactive controls reachable and activatable without a pointer.
- **Visible focus** — `:focus-visible` outline or equivalent; never `outline: none` without a replacement.
- **Name** — every control has an accessible name (visible label, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby`).
- **Role** — use native semantics first; ARIA roles only when native elements insufficient.
- **Color contrast** — text and meaningful UI icons ≥ 4.5:1 (normal text) / 3:1 (large text/UI components) against background in themed mode.
- **Motion** — honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` (disable non-essential animation/transitions).
- **Touch targets** — interactive targets ≥ 24×24 CSS px where practical (WCAG 2.2 2.5.8).

## Component-kind patterns

### Accordion / collapsible

- Header is a **`<button type="button">`** (not `<div onclick>`).
- `aria-expanded` reflects open state.
- `aria-controls` points to panel id when panel exists.
- Enter and Space toggle; optional Arrow keys between headers in a group.

### Tabs

- Tab list: `role="tablist"`; tabs: `role="tab"` with `aria-selected`.
- Panels: `role="tabpanel"`, `aria-labelledby` linked to tab.
- Arrow Left/Right (horizontal) or Up/Down (vertical) move focus between tabs; activation follows WAI-ARIA tabs pattern.

### Modal / dialog

- `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal="true"`.
- Focus trap while open; restore focus to trigger on close.
- Escape closes unless explicitly disabled.
- Background scroll locked while modal open.

### Select / listbox / combobox

- Follow WAI-ARIA APG for the chosen pattern.
- Typeahead where list length > 10 items.
- Selected state exposed to assistive tech.

### Text inputs / textarea / checkbox / number

- Native `<input>`, `<textarea>`, `<select>` preferred.
- Associate `<label>` or `aria-label`; expose `aria-invalid` + error text when validation fails.
- Do not rely on placeholder as sole label.

### Date range

- Provide accessible names for start/end fields.
- Announce range changes if programmatically updated (`aria-live="polite"` on summary region).

### Data table

- Use `<table>` with `<th scope="col|row">` for tabular data.
- Sortable columns: `aria-sort` on header button.
- Row selection: checkbox column with header label.

### Charts (bar, line, pie, 3D bar)

- Root: `role="img"` with meaningful **`aria-label`** summarizing the data (not just "Bar chart").
- Provide **text alternative**: visually hidden `<table>` or description list with the same data when data is known.
- Decorative-only charts in demos must still have a label stating they are illustrative.

### KPI / metric

- Value + label association via heading or `aria-labelledby`.
- Trend/delta communicated in text, not color alone.

### 3D / globe / map

- Container: `aria-label` describing purpose (e.g. "Interactive globe showing destination markers").
- **Non-visual fallback required**: list/table of markers or destinations with same select/action affordances.
- Do not make pointer-only interaction the only path to core functionality.

### Video / media

- `<video>` controls must be keyboard accessible when native controls shown.
- Autoplay requires `muted` + user expectation documented; never autoplay with sound.
- YouTube embed: title on iframe; provide alternative link to content.
- Live regions for processing states (`aria-live="polite"` on wasm progress).

### Loading / skeleton / empty / error

- Loading: `aria-busy="true"` on region or `role="status"` with visible text ("Loading…").
- Empty: text explaining empty state, not blank silence.
- Error: `role="alert"` or `aria-live="assertive"` for critical failures.

## Async updates

- Filter results, timer ticks, wasm progress: use `aria-live="polite"` unless user action requires immediate attention (`assertive`).
- Do not move focus unexpectedly on data refresh.

## Builder palette (related)

Palette accordion headers in the builder app must be buttons with `aria-expanded` — see `apps/client/.cursor/rules/builder-app.mdc`. Public `rd-*` components follow the patterns above.

## Acceptance checklist (before merge)

- [ ] Keyboard path documented in Storybook story description
- [ ] Focus order logical; no keyboard traps except modals
- [ ] All interactive elements named
- [ ] Color not sole indicator of state
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` respected
- [ ] Chart/3D/map has text alternative
- [ ] Spec or Storybook `play` function covers at least one keyboard interaction where applicable

